WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
Two pupils translate "I see nothing".

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.490
One writes: Veo nada.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.030
The other writes: No veo nada.

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.050
That second version has
two negatives in it:

5
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.070
"not" and "nothing".

6
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.490
In standard English, a double
negative like "I don't see

7
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.810
nothing" is marked wrong.

8
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.290
So which pupil got the Spanish right?

9
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.720
In this mission, you'll learn
where to put the word for "not".

10
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:30.050
You'll meet three negative
words: nada, nunca, nadie.

11
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.010
And you'll find out when
Spanish lets you drop the "not"

12
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.410
altogether.

13
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.490
Your mission: decide which
pupil got it right, and why.
